      "title": "The master rule",
      "narration": "Rosa asks whether her disability benefits will be taxed. The answer to almost every health insurance tax question is the same: follow the premium. If the premium was paid with after-tax dollars and never deducted, the benefit is tax-free. If the premium was deducted, excluded from income or paid by an employer, the benefit is taxable, except where Congress made a specific exception, as it did for medical expense reimbursements. Learn that rule, then learn the exceptions. For individually owned coverage the premium is almost always after-tax, so benefits are almost always tax-free; the question is only whether the premium itself can be deducted.",
