      "narration": "A health savings account is the most tax-favored of the three accounts. Rosa’s contributions are deductible, or excluded from pay if made through payroll; earnings grow untaxed; withdrawals for qualified medical expenses are tax-free; and the balance is hers for life. Nonqualified withdrawals are taxed and, before 65, penalized 20 percent. A health reimbursement arrangement is funded only by the employer, whose contributions are deductible business expenses and are not income to the employee; reimbursements for medical expenses are tax-free. The employee contributes nothing, so there is no deduction to claim and nothing to penalize.",
